/-!
# The norm of a finite group action

The norm `TauCeti.groupNorm G M` sums the scalar translates of an element of an additive
commutative monoid. Its definition needs only distributive scalar multiplication by the finite
scalar type. For a finite normal subgroup of a group acting on `M`, the norm commutes with the
ambient action and is bundled as the equivariant additive map `TauCeti.groupNormHom`.

For a finite cyclic group generated by `g`, `TauCeti.groupNorm_eq_sum_range` expresses the norm
as the sum over `1, g, …, gⁿ⁻¹`, where `n = orderOf g`. This formula applies without a ring of
scalars or a representation.
-/

public section

namespace TauCeti

-- Backport note: `groupNorm`, `groupNorm_apply`, `groupNorm_smul`, `groupNormHom` and
-- `groupNormHom_apply` (identical statements) are taken from the oct16 module
-- `GroupCohomology.Cocycle`, where they lived before moving to this file at nov01.

/-- The norm of a finite cyclic group is the sum of the translates by powers of a generator.
Only distributive scalar multiplication on an additive commutative monoid is required. -/
theorem groupNorm_eq_sum_range {G M : Type*} [Group G] [Fintype G] [AddCommMonoid M]
    [DistribSMul G M] (g : G) (hg : ∀ x : G, x ∈ Subgroup.zpowers g) (m : M) :
    groupNorm G M m = ∑ i ∈ Finset.range (orderOf g), g ^ i • m := by
  rw [groupNorm_apply]
  exact (sum_range_orderOf_eq_sum g hg (fun x ↦ x • m)).symm

end TauCeti
